 people the real  side of language learning that i kind of  want  this idea of me as a polyglot that i'm  not impressive i don't want people to  think i'm smart i want people to be able  to do  what i've done because anyone can do it  it's just a case of finding the right  approach  and i'm hoping my advice will help you  out with that so  fluent in three months or irish polyglot  do a search for those or language  hacking podcast  thank you i think it's impressive  regardless uh i remember i was in  you mentioned how people around the  world speak multiple languages and it's  really just english people that think  no it's just one language you know per  person and i was in switzerland  and i was in a cab or an uber i was in  an uber  and he was talking to me and then he had  two phone calls and each phone call was  in a different language and i was like  how many languages do you speak and he's  like oh he's six fluently  and he's an uber driver in switzerland  and he's like how many do you speak and  it was just like  one he was like oh it's like yeah that's  you know it's not just me i swear it's  not just me  but thank you thank you very much for  coming on that was really interesting  uh and best of luck with your russian  and i re i really hope i've shown you  that  you absolutely can learn it i've i  started  in my 20s and now i'm i'm a polyglot and  a lot of people  who follow my stuff have started much  much later in life and they've succeeded  so it's never too late to learn a  language that is  so cool thank you very much thank you  you


